<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/talks-ted-processing-units> {
  ex:ted-processing-step a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "What does one processing step do?"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-processing-step-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-processing-step-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A processing step accepts input data, performs a defined task and produces output data. Parameters configure the transformation. Input and output are distinct from the algorithm that implements the task. Describing that interface lets a person or another tool determine what can be supplied and what the result means. The schematic is conceptual, not a running operation or a claim that all processing has exactly one input and one output."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-composable-steps a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "An output becomes the next input"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-composable-steps-definition ; skos:related ex:cogniflow-processing-pipeline ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-composable-steps-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "A pipeline explicitly connects specialized processing steps. Each step has a defined task; a produced result can supply a following step's input only when their interface contracts are compatible. Matching file extensions or port names alone is insufficient: meaning, data types, structure, units and applicable constraints must agree, or an explicit conversion is needed. The illustrated TED excerpt detects features in EICs, jointly fits compatible features into components, and selects marker components. It does not claim to show the whole pipeline or to replace its import and external calibration steps."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-processing-unit a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "A shared model, a concrete operation"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-processing-unit-definition ; skos:related ex:cogniflow-domain-specifications ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-processing-unit-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "In the shared workshop model, ProcessingUnit is the reusable processing abstraction. It exposes Port attributes, with PortRole values Input, Output and Parameter. ProcessingStep is an atomic specialization; ProcessingPipeline is a composite specialization, composed through PipelineNodes whose RunTarget identifies the ProcessingUnit being run. Both can expose the same kind of interface. Describe port meaning using shared, defined vocabulary, together with data type, structure, units, cardinality and validity constraints where relevant. The input contract describes what is required; the output contract describes what is produced. A compatible output can be connected to a subsequent input. First explain this public contract, then the algorithm, parameters, software version and execution provenance behind it. This is an explanatory order, not an exemption from documenting implementation or a claim that standardized ports alone make processing FAIR or reproducible. The three-column diagram distinguishes the shared concept model, its atomic/composite specializations, and the concrete qalg:Average operation with declared ports and a service binding. Its arrows summarize specialization and specification, not data flow, execution order or the direction of subClassOf assertions."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-processing-unit ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:ted-step-points a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "A defined transformation connects input and output."@en ; cd:hasKeyPoint ex:ted-step-p1, ex:ted-step-p2, ex:ted-step-p3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-step-p1 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "**Input:** the data a step receives"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-step-p2 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "**Process:** one defined task transforms the data"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-step-p3 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "**Output:** the result the step produces"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-chain-points a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Specialized steps compose through compatible interfaces."@en ; cd:hasKeyPoint ex:ted-chain-p1, ex:ted-chain-p2, ex:ted-chain-p3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-chain-p1 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "**Each step:** one defined task"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-chain-p2 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "**Connect:** an output supplies a following input"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-chain-p3 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "==Compatible meaning, not just matching file names=="@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-unit-points a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Standardize the public contract, then describe its implementation."@en ; cd:hasKeyPoint ex:ted-unit-p1, ex:ted-unit-p2, ex:ted-unit-p3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-unit-p1 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "**Model:** shared concepts, ports and roles"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-unit-p2 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "**Specialize:** atomic step or composite pipeline"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:ted-unit-p3 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "**Specify:** concrete ports, then bind an implementation"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/sources/talks-ted-processing-units> {
  ex:ted-source-processing-unit a cd:Source ; dct:title "Workshop: ProcessingUnit, Port roles and pipeline composition" ; dct:creator "Gerrit Renner" ; dct:identifier "speaker-supplied-workshop#cf-concept-domain-diagram" ; dct:hasVersion "sha256:b188e0a56a92d6872e1d013b82260ac97cacbd84d1ee8a866fb37526618c0725" ; dct:description "Supplied workshop diagram: ProcessingUnit; Port; PortRole with Input, Output and Parameter; ProcessingStep and ProcessingPipeline as specializations; PipelineNode and runs targeting a ProcessingUnit. Teaching adaptation aligns with existing canonical domain and pipeline definitions. No historical core hasAttribute syntax is imported as a new canonical ontology contract."@en ; cd:supportsResource ex:ted-processing-step-definition, ex:ted-composable-steps-definition, ex:ted-processing-unit-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
